# XCU delta
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# SCCS files are made and inspected only with the SCCS utilities (admin,
# get, delta, prs and friends); the file format is unspecified so nothing
# reads the files directly. A missing companion utility makes the test
# UNRESOLVED. Login names, dates and the diagnostic texts are never compared
# literally.

assertion  XCU.delta.001
anchor     utilities/delta.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/delta.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       delta prints the new SID and the inserted, deleted and unchanged
           line counts; the g-file is removed, the new version is what get
           retrieves, the old one remains available, and another get -e is
           allowed afterwards.
test       t/001-report-and-remove.sh

assertion  XCU.delta.002
anchor     utilities/delta.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -s suppresses the report and -n keeps the edited g-file.
test       t/002-options-s-n.sh

assertion  XCU.delta.003
anchor     utilities/delta.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/delta.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       Replacing one line of three reports one inserted, one deleted and
           two unchanged, and the -y text becomes the delta comment.
test       t/003-counts-comment.sh

assertion  XCU.delta.004
anchor     utilities/delta.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -p writes the differences in diff format to standard output.
test       t/004-diff-output.sh

assertion  XCU.delta.005
anchor     utilities/delta.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       delta on a file with no pending edit gives a non-zero status and
           changes nothing.
test       t/005-no-pending-edit.sh

assertion  XCU.delta.006
anchor     utilities/delta.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/delta.html#STDIN
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       A single - operand reads SCCS file names from standard input,
           with -y supplying the comment.
test       t/006-stdin-names.sh

assertion  XCU.delta.007
anchor     utilities/delta.html#OPTIONS/-r
class      required
since      1992
says       With two outstanding edits by the same user, -r with either the
           SID given to get or the SID to be made picks which one delta
           completes.
test       t/007-r-two-edits.sh

assertion  XCU.delta.008
anchor     utilities/delta.html#OPTIONS/-g
class      required
since      1992
says       Deltas named by -g are ignored when the file is later accessed at
           the level of the new delta.
test       t/008-g-ignore.sh

assertion  XCU.delta.009
anchor     utilities/delta.html#OPTIONS/-m
class      required
since      1992
says       When the v flag names a validation program, -m MR numbers are
           accepted and recorded when it exits zero, and when it exits
           non-zero delta terminates without adding a delta.
test       t/009-m-validator.sh

assertion  XCU.delta.010
anchor     utilities/delta.html#OPTIONS/-y
anchor     utilities/delta.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       -y with no comment is a valid null comment; without -y the
           "comments? " prompt is written to standard output when standard
           input is a terminal and the typed line becomes the comment, and
           no prompt is written when it is not.
test       t/010-prompt-and-null-comment.sh
